<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh SEC files law suits over stock fraud.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh SEC files law suits over stock fraud.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) on Wednesday filed cases against 15 companies and several brokers and dealers for their alleged involvement &quot;in fraudulent acts responsible for unusual ups and downs&quot; in share market causing losses to investors, the official BSS news agency said.</p>
<p>It said the cases were filed at the court of Dhaka's chief metropolitan magistrate &quot;on the basis of a report of a four-member inquiry committtee headed by Professor Aminul Islam.&quot;</p>
</text>
